diff --git a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e8530e4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+MT6762 early-boot research machine
+=================================
+
+This local experimental machine is named ``mt6762``. It is not a complete
+MediaTek SoC or phone emulator. Its address map comes from the supplied
+MT6762 phone firmware, whose device tree uses the MT6765 family name.
+This code is an AI-assisted local experiment and is not intended for
+submission to upstream QEMU.
+
+Implemented resources
+---------------------
+
+* One to eight Cortex-A53 CPUs, MPIDRs 0--3 and 0x100--0x103.
+* RAM at 0x40000000, configurable with ``-m``; 512 MiB is the static DTB
+  placeholder, not an assertion of the phone's installed capacity.
+* GICv3 distributor at 0x0c000000 and redistributors at 0x0c100000.
+* Architectural timer at 13 MHz, PPIs 29/30/27/26.
+* Two 16550-compatible UART register subsets at 0x11002000 and
+  0x11003000 with 32-bit register spacing, SPIs 91/92.
+* QEMU PSCI via SMC, direct Linux Image boot into nonsecure EL1.
+* Interrupt polarity register bank at 0x10200a80. QEMU device interrupt
+  wires represent logical assertion, so connected UART/timer outputs are
+  already normalized; the bank preserves guest polarity programming.
+* MediaTek 13 MHz one-shot broadcast timer at 0x10017000, control/value
+  registers at offsets 0x40/0x44, SPI 194. Its programming sequence comes
+  from the supplied BSP's ``drivers/clocksource/mtk_systimer.c``.
+
+The MediaTek UART extension registers,
+clock/reset/power controllers, PMIC, eMMC, USB, display, GPU, touch, modem,
+TEE and boot firmware are not emulated. Unmapped accesses remain unmapped;
+they are not silently replaced with successful handshakes.
+
+Usage
+-----
+
+A device tree is mandatory. The stock extracted DTB is useful for showing
+the exact first unsupported dependency in the unmodified stock kernel::
+
+  qemu-system-aarch64 -M mt6762 -accel tcg -cpu cortex-a53 -smp 8 -m 512M \
+    -display none -monitor none -serial stdio -no-reboot \
+    -kernel Image -dtb boot.bin.dtb \
+    -append 'earlycon=uart8250,mmio32,0x11002000 keep_bootcon ignore_loglevel nokaslr maxcpus=1'
+
+``maxcpus=1`` is a debugging choice: the machine still exposes the full
+topology, while Linux initially uses one CPU. The generic device loader
+can place additional XNU segments or boot data in RAM for trampoline
+experiments. Neither an early serial message nor a successful CPU probe
+establishes that Android or iOS boots.
+
+Observed stock-kernel boundary
+-----------------------------
+
+The supplied Linux 4.19.191 Image reaches its init kernel thread, with
+working GICv3 and architectural timer interrupts. It then faults in
+``log_store_early_init``. The extracted DTB lacks the bootloader's runtime
+handoff for SRAM logging (the kernel reports SRAM address/size zero).
+Bootloader handoff, SRAM and the remaining vendor devices need further
+modeling. There is no userspace or full Android boot yet.
